one las vegas man contacted us at  channel 8 about what he discovered on a  private golf course a homeless camp well  the itunes vanessa murphy has more on  what she found and why there is  confusion about cleaning up the area  the las vegas national golf course is  minutes from the strip  i mean it's peaceful and quiet houses  like these border the property  you know you just look out your back  window and  you know that pretty much says it right  there herbert bashar says he's a  caretaker at this home on  ottawa street it's a great environment  to be around the nature  here but what he also found and i was  absolutely shocked  trash blankets and during our visit  someone  who appeared to be sleeping in this tent  this is somebody's home complete with  the outdoor barbecue grill  the golf course is surrounded by a fence  bashar tells us he's seen individuals  here on spencer use this  bookcase to step here and hop over  but during our visit we see one gate  wide open  this is is not the sanctuary  for homeless people the i-team reached  out to the las vegas national golf  course  general manager coy wood told us over  the phone  the golf course just doesn't have the  resources to keep up with the issue  in an email he wrote it's quote an  ongoing problem that we have been trying  to get the county to help control for  the past six to seven years with no help  end quote and in regards to the homeless  police will help try to remove them  only if there is a threat to workers  it's certainly an  issue and it's not going to go away the  i-team also contacted clark county  spokesman dan kulin says this is private  property and responsibility falls  on the golf course he also tells the  i-team the county is responsible for  this fence  and after we told him it was open the  county would check  on it while there is a disagreement on  who should  clean this up the gm says any help from  the public would be greatly  appreciated vanessa murphy 8 news now  we have the full response from the las  vegas national golf course on our  website 8newsnow.com
 

